Sure! However, I need a bit more information to assist you accurately. What type of button are you looking to create? Here are a few examples:

1. **HTML Button**:
   ```html
   <button type="button">Click Me!</button>
   ```

2. **Styled Button with CSS**:
   ```html
   <button class="my-button">Click Me!</button>

   <style>
       .my-button {
           background-color: #4CAF50; /* Green */
           border: none;
           color: white;
           padding: 15px 32px;
           text-align: center;
           text-decoration: none;
           display: inline-block;
           font-size: 16px;
           margin: 4px 2px;
           cursor: pointer;
           border-radius: 12px;
       }
   </style>
   ```

3. **JavaScript Functionality**:
   ```html
   <button onclick="myFunction()">Click Me!</button>

   <script>
       function myFunction() {
           alert('Button was clicked!');
       }
   </script>
   ```

4. **React Button Component**:
   ```javascript
   import React from 'react';

   function MyButton() {
       const handleClick = () => {
           alert('Button was clicked!');
       };

       return (
           <button onClick={handleClick}>Click Me!</button>
       );
   }

   export default MyButton;
   ```

